// Session services, ported from the wayblue sway drop-in 90-keyring.conf.
//
// The wayblue niri image has no equivalent of that drop-in, so without this
// the Secret portal and anything relying on the keyring silently stops working
// after the sway -> niri switch.
//
// `dbus-update-activation-environment` is deliberately *not* ported: niri
// already pushes the session environment into systemd and D-Bus itself when
// started via `niri --session` (i.e. through niri-session / the display
// manager).
//
// The spawn is guarded so a missing binary is a no-op instead of a startup
// error in the niri log.

spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "command -v gnome-keyring-daemon >/dev/null 2>&1 && exec gnome-keyring-daemon --start --components=secrets"
